              "content": "#!/bin/bash\n# Flux job script translated from PBS\n\n# WARNING: The original script contains placeholder values (FIXME).\n# These must be replaced with actual values before submitting the job.\n\n#flux: -q FIXME                       # queue allocation\n\n# The original script did not specify tasks or cpus, so it defaults to a single task with one CPU.\n# This is preserved in the Flux script.\n#flux: -N 1 # Assuming a single node as nodes=FIXME\n#flux: -n 1\n#flux: -c 1\n\n# The PBS output directive is preserved.\n#flux: -o OpenMM.err\n\n#flux: --job-name=5Y2S_GPU_OpenMM\n\n# CRITICAL: The original PBS script had a placeholder for GPU info ('nodes=FIXME').\n# This translation assumes a GPU is required based on the script's content (CUDA, OpenMM).\n# However, no specific GPU request can be made as there is no standard Flux directive.\n# This job will likely FAIL unless submitted to a queue configured to provide a GPU.\n\n# The PBS '-j oe' (combine output/error) and '-r n' (not rerunnable) are default or untranslatable.\n\n\n## If you get a segfalt error and you're a TINKER user\n## add the .bashrc_blank file to $HOME on Cruntch and \n## uncomment this line.\n#source ~/.bashrc_blank\n\n## The specific GPU card to use\n## Change \"0\" to the one you want\nexport CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0\n\n## Go to the directory that the job was submitted from\n# FLUX_SUBMIT_DIR is the equivalent of PBS_O_WORKDIR\ncd $FLUX_SUBMIT_DIR\n\n## Load OpenMM\n## K80s use CUDA 8.0, V100s use CUDA 10.0\nmodule load openmm/cuda-8.0\n#module load openmm/cuda-10.0\n\n## Run the Python Script and print Terminal output to file\n# The command is run directly. As a single-task job, 'flux run' is not necessary.\npython new_openmm_simulations.py\n"
