      "slurm": "#!/bin/bash\n# Flux batch script converted from Cobalt\n\n# NOTE: Run with: flux batch <this_script> -- <nodes> <ranks_per_node> <threads_per_core> [app args...]\n\n# Omitted Cobalt option: -A CSC249ADCD08\n# Flux accounting/project selection is site-specific; no portable equivalent.\n# Performance implication: job may be charged to a default account or rejected by policy.\n\n# Omitted Cobalt option: --attrs enable_ssh=1\n# Flux has no universal, portable equivalent for Cobalt job attributes.\n# Performance implication: SSH into allocated nodes may not be enabled, which can hinder debugging/interactive inspection.\n\n# Dynamic resource calculation based on script arguments\nnodes=$1\nranks_per_node=$2\nthreads_per_core=$3\n\nif [ -z \"$nodes\" ] || [ -z \"$ranks_per_node\" ] || [ -z \"$threads_per_core\" ]; then\n  echo \"Usage: $0 <nodes> <ranks_per_node> <threads_per_core> [app args...]\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\ntotal_ranks=$((nodes * ranks_per_node))\nthreads_per_rank=$(((64 * threads_per_core) / ranks_per_node))\n\n# Request resources (must come after argument parsing for dynamic values)\n#flux: -N ${nodes}\n#flux: -n ${total_ranks}\n#flux: -c ${threads_per_rank}\n\n# Load up the Python environment\nmodule load miniconda-3/latest\nsource activate /lus/theta-fs0/projects/CSC249ADCD08/design/graph_sage/env\nexport PYTHONPATH=\"\"  ## Get rid of the default path from the modules\n\n# Environment\nexport KMP_BLOCKTIME=0\nexport KMP_AFFINITY=\"granularity=fine,compact,1,0\"\nexport MPICH_GNI_FORK_MODE=FULLCOPY\nexport OMP_NUM_THREADS=$threads_per_rank\n\n# Cobalt used aprun (-n total_ranks, -N ranks_per_node, -d threads, -j threads_per_core, --cc depth)\n# In Flux, use flux-run to launch ranks across the allocation.\n# Omitted aprun option: -N (ranks per node), -j (threads per core), and --cc depth (core binding policy)\n# Flux rank placement/binding is configuration-dependent.\n# Performance implication: without explicit per-node placement and binding, MPI ranks/threads may be mapped suboptimally, reducing performance.\n\nflux run -n ${total_ranks} -c ${threads_per_rank} \\\n  --env=KMP_BLOCKTIME \\\n  --env=KMP_AFFINITY \\\n  --env=MPICH_GNI_FORK_MODE \\\n  --env=OMP_NUM_THREADS \\\n  python profile_train.py ${@:4}\n\n```\n\n### REQUIREMENTS & CONSTRAINTS\nYou MUST return a JSON structure with fields for 'valid' (bool) and a list of string 'reasons'. You MAY optionally add a field `issues` with a list of debugging or critique of any code.\n\n### INSTRUCTIONS\n1. Analyze the provided script above.\n2. Use MUST use a jobspec validation tool for the manager if one is available otherwise use your knowledge.\n3. Determine validity based on the resource section ONLY\n4. The 'reasons' should ONLY be specific to resources\n5. If the script includes problematic code, please include in 'issues'\n6. You MUST include a 'tool_call' boolean, true or false, to indicate if you used a validation tool for validation.\n7. Return a json structure with 'valid' and 'tool_call' and 'reasons' (if not valid) and 'issues'",
      "flux": "#!/bin/bash\n# Flux batch script converted from Cobalt\n\n# NOTE:\n#   Flux batch directives (#flux:) must be static (no shell variable expansion).\n#   Therefore this script cannot take <nodes> <ranks_per_node> <threads_per_core>\n#   as runtime parameters *and* express them in #flux: directives.\n#\n# How to use instead:\n#   Set NODES, RANKS_PER_NODE, THREADS_PER_CORE below, then run:\n#     flux batch <this_script>\n\n# ---- User-settable resources (static) ----\nNODES=1\nRANKS_PER_NODE=1\nTHREADS_PER_CORE=1\n# ----------------------------------------\n\nTOTAL_RANKS=$((NODES * RANKS_PER_NODE))\nTHREADS_PER_RANK=$(((64 * THREADS_PER_CORE) / RANKS_PER_NODE))\n\n# Cobalt: aprun -n $total_ranks ...\n# Map to Flux: allocate nodes and total tasks; allocate cores per task for threading.\n#flux: -N 1\n#flux: -n 1\n#flux: -c 64\n\n# Omitted Cobalt option: -A CSC249ADCD08\n# Flux accounting/project selection is site-specific; no portable equivalent.\n# Performance implication: job may be charged to a default account or rejected by policy.\n\n# Omitted Cobalt option: --attrs enable_ssh=1\n# Flux has no universal, portable equivalent for Cobalt job attributes.\n# Performance implication: SSH into allocated nodes may not be enabled, which can hinder debugging/interactive inspection.\n\n# Omitted aprun options: -N (ranks per node), -j (threads per core), --cc depth (binding)\n# Flux placement/binding controls are site/config dependent and not expressed portably here.\n# Performance implication: rank/thread placement may be suboptimal, reducing performance.\n\n# Load up the Python environment\nmodule load miniconda-3/latest\nsource activate /lus/theta-fs0/projects/CSC249ADCD08/design/graph_sage/env\nexport PYTHONPATH=\"\"  ## Get rid of the default path from the modules\n\n# Environment\nexport KMP_BLOCKTIME=0\nexport KMP_AFFINITY=\"granularity=fine,compact,1,0\"\nexport MPICH_GNI_FORK_MODE=FULLCOPY\nexport OMP_NUM_THREADS=$THREADS_PER_RANK\n\n# Launch across allocated resources\nflux run -n $TOTAL_RANKS -c $THREADS_PER_RANK \\\n  --env=KMP_BLOCKTIME \\\n  --env=KMP_AFFINITY \\\n  --env=MPICH_GNI_FORK_MODE \\\n  --env=OMP_NUM_THREADS \\\n  python profile_train.py ${@:4}\n",
