              "content": "#!/bin/bash\n\n# Flux batch script converted from PBS\n# Note: Flux does not support in-script directives for resource specification\n# This script should be submitted with the following command:\n# flux batch -N 1 -n 1 -t 100h --job-name=bead-select --output=bead-select-{{id}}.out --error=bead-select-{{id}}.err --array=0-1024 script.sh\n#\n# Resource specifications:\n# -N 1         : 1 node (from procs=1)\n# -n 1         : 1 task (from procs=1)\n# -t 100h      : 100 hour walltime (from walltime=100:00:00)\n# --job-name=bead-select : job name (from -N bead-select)\n# --array=0-1024 : array job indices 0-1024 (from -t 0-1024)\n#\n# Note: Memory specification (mem=7GB) should be added at submission:\n# Add: --setattr=system.memory=7168M (7 * 1024 MB)\n# Complete command:\n# flux batch -N 1 -n 1 -t 100h --job-name=bead-select --setattr=system.memory=7168M --array=0-1024 script.sh\n\n# Original PBS job name: bead-select\n# Flux: --job-name=bead-select\n\n# Original PBS procs: 1\n# Flux: -N 1 -n 1 (1 node, 1 task)\n\n# Original PBS walltime: 100:00:00 (100 hours)\n# Flux: -t 100h or -t 6000m or -t 360000s\n\n# Original PBS memory: 7GB\n# Note: Flux memory specification uses --setattr\n# Memory should be specified at submission:\n# flux batch --setattr=system.memory=7168M ... (7 * 1024 MB)\n# Or: --setattr=system.memory=7G (if supported by Flux version)\n# Performance impact: Without explicit memory specification, job may get default allocation\n# which could be insufficient for this workload\n\n# Original PBS queue: WitsLong\n# Note: Flux does not have queues in the same way as PBS\n# Queue/partition selection is handled through Flux's scheduling configuration\n# Performance impact: Job scheduling priority depends on site-specific Flux configuration\n# Consult site documentation for equivalent resource pools or priority settings\n\n# Original PBS array: -t 0-1024\n# Flux: --array=0-1024 at submission time\n# Note: PBS_ARRAYID becomes FLUX_TASK_ID in Flux\n# Array job indices: 0-1024 (1025 jobs total)\n\nhostname\n\ncd /spaces/scott/chip/pool_selection/\n\n# PBS uses PBS_ARRAYID, Flux uses FLUX_TASK_ID\nrun=${FLUX_TASK_ID}\n\n/usr/bin/time python pool_select.py --input all.cpickle --label S${LABEL} --bad badscore60.lst --requests extra.lst,req_func_u.scores --factor 1.5 $run 10 18\n\n# Note on array job environment variables:\n# PBS: PBS_ARRAYID provides the array index\n# Flux: FLUX_TASK_ID provides the array task index\n# Both provide the current index in the array job\n\n# Complete submission command with all options:\n# flux batch -N 1 -n 1 -t 100h \\\n#   --job-name=bead-select \\\n#   --output=bead-select-{{id}}.out \\\n#   --error=bead-select-{{id}}.err \\\n#   --setattr=system.memory=7168M \\\n#   --array=0-1024 \\\n#   script.sh\n#\n# Note: Flux uses {{id}} for job ID in output filenames\n# The array index can be accessed via FLUX_TASK_ID within the script\n"
